                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \,\in\, sSet
              there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi ℭ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi 𝒢
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L \circ \mathfrak{C}(S)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\mathcal{G}(S)
            %p
              which is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dwyer-Kan+equivalence"} Dwyer-Kan equivalence
              (from the localization
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:LocalizationOfsSetCategoriesToSSetGroupoids"} (1)
              of the rigidification
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:RigidificationOfQuasiCategories"} (2)
              to the Dwyer-Kan fundamental groupoid (as
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Definition"} above
          \&amp;lbrack;
          %a{:href => "#MinichielloRiveraZeinalian23"}> Minichiello, Rivera &amp; Zeinalian (2023), Thm. 1.1 (Cor. 4.2)
          \&amp;rbrack;
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The original reference for the functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is Section 9 in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+M.+Kan"}> Daniel M. Kan
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A combinatorial definition of homotopy groups
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/1970006"} doi:10.2307/1970006
          %p
            Later, Dwyer and Kan constructed the right adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar W
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            in
          %ul
            %li#DwyerKan84
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Dwyer"}> William Dwyer
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Kan"} Daniel Kan
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homotopy theory and simplicial groupoids
              %strong 87
              4 (1984) 379-385 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/1385-7258(84)90038-6"}> doi:10.1016/1385-7258(84)90038-6
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p#ReferencesBeware
            Beware that the definition in
            %a{:href => "#DwyerKan84"} Dwyer &amp; Kan (1984) §3.1
            apparently contains a mistake (in its formula for
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_0
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andre+Joyal"} Joyal
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Myles+Tierney"} Tierney
          %ul
            %li#Ehlers91
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Philip+Ehlers"}> Philip Ehlers
              , pp. 10 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Simplicial groupoids as models for homotopy type
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/Ehlers-MSc-thesis.pdf"} pdf
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li#JoyalTierney00
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"}> André Joyal
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Myles+Tierney"} Myles Tierney
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the theory of path groupoids
                %strong 149
                1 (2000) 69-100 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-4049(98)00164-9"}> doi:10.1016/S0022-4049(98)00164-9
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#GoerssJardine09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Goerss"}> Paul Goerss
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+F.+Jardine"} J. F. Jardine
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simplicial+homotopy+theory"} Simplicial homotopy theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-0346-0189-4"} doi:10.1007/978-3-0346-0189-4
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://web.archive.org/web/19990208220238/http://www.math.uwo.ca/~jardine/papers/simp-sets/"} webpage
          %p
            Relating the Dwyer-Kan loop groupoid-construction to the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rigidification+of+quasi-categories"} rigidification of quasi-categories
          %ul
            %li#MinichielloRiveraZeinalian23
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emilio+Minichiello"}> Emilio Minichiello
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Manuel+Rivera"} Manuel Rivera
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mahmoud+Zeinalian"} Mahmoud Zeinalian
              = succeed "," do
                %em Categorical models for path spaces
              %strong 415
              (2023) 108898 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.03046"}> arXiv:2201.03046
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aim.2023.108898"} doi:10.1016/j.aim.2023.108898
        .revisedby
